        "department": null,
        "description": "This course is designed for advanced graduate and PhD students. It is reading and writing intensive. This seminar style course will familiarize students with the political, social, and ethical aspects of data science practices. Leveraging epistemic traditions of Information Science and Social Informatics, and incorporating a variety case studies and contexts, the course aims to educate students to be reflective thinkers and practitioners. Students will learn to critically evaluate the processes of collecting, aggregating, and analyzing data, and apply this knowledge to develop data-driven strategies and policies that are relevant both globally and locally (in India).",
